# Build artifacts
fortran/*.so
fortran/*.o
*.mod
fortran/_sacsma_patched/

# Extracted from external/snow17/test_cases/ex1.tgz at test time
external/snow17/test_cases/ex1/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# CAMELS data: downloaded via data/download_camels.sh, not committed
# (the forcing+flow archive alone is ~3.4GB, ~14GB extracted). Ignore
# everything under data/camels/ except the one small, human-readable,
# reproducible-from-a-fixed-seed reference worth keeping in the repo:
# selected_basins.csv (which basins we used, and why -- frac_snow etc).
# basin_attributes.npz is regenerated by data/build_attributes.py in
# seconds from the (untracked, re-downloadable) attribute text files --
# not tracked despite being small, since it's binary/undiffable and
# fully reproducible.
data/camels/*
!data/camels/selected_basins.csv

# src/train.py's default output_dir is timestamped
# (results/runs/<model>_<split>_<timestamp>/) -- exploratory runs
# shouldn't accumulate in git. The two canonical, reproducible reference
# runs (results/README.md) are explicitly kept.
results/runs/*
!results/runs/hybrid_spatial_seed0/
!results/runs/benchmark_lstm_spatial_seed0/
results/predictions/

# Hydra's own bookkeeping (config.yaml, overrides.yaml, hydra.yaml,
# <job>.log) nests inside each run's output_dir (configs/config.yaml's
# hydra.run.dir) -- ignored wherever a run happens to land, as a
# safety net in case output_dir is ever overridden to somewhere untracked.
.hydra/
*.log

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
